WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:16.803
At last Buldeo finished telling his stories.

2
00:00:16.804 --> 00:00:19.935
The villagers left the fig tree.

3
00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:24.309
They rushed toward Messua's hut, waving clubs and knives.

4
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.881
They all carried torches.

5
00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:33.785
"Let's burn down the sorcerers' hut!" people yelled angrily.

6
00:00:33.786 --> 00:00:37.693
The crowd reached the hut and tore off the door.

7
00:00:37.694 --> 00:00:43.003
Everyone expected to see Messua and her husband trapped inside.

8
00:00:43.004 --> 00:00:50.434
Instead, stretched out on the bed with his paws crossed, was a fierce black panther.

9
00:00:50.435 --> 00:00:55.099
Bagheera slowly raised his head, flashing sharp white teeth.

10
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.964
The villagers screamed.

11
00:00:57.965 --> 00:01:02.526
Then, in a panic, they scrambled to get outside.

12
00:01:02.527 --> 00:01:07.853
They raced to their huts and slammed shut the doors.

13
00:01:07.854 --> 00:01:11.603
Mowgli stepped out of the shadows and grinned.

14
00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.675
"That was a good plan, Bagheera!"

15
00:01:14.676 --> 00:01:19.432
"Thank you," the panther said proudly as he licked his paws.

16
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:25.917
"The villagers won't come out until daylight. Let's get some rest now."

17
00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:31.468
When Mowgli woke the next day, he saw Rann, the hawk.

18
00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:35.338
"I have a message from Mother Wolf," the bird called.

19
00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:42.353
"Messua and her husband are safe in the new village. It is near a marsh."

20
00:01:42.354 --> 00:01:52.658
Mowgli waved happily. "Thank you!" Then he went off to tell Bagheera.

21
00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:56.637
"The people are still huddled indoors," Bagheera said.

22
00:01:56.638 --> 00:02:00.005
"Why don't we go hunting and forget about them?"

23
00:02:00.006 --> 00:02:02.128
Mowgli shook his head.

24
00:02:02.129 --> 00:02:06.454
"I'm sorry, Bagheera. I have to finish what I started.

25
00:02:06.455 --> 00:02:08.890
It's the law of the jungle.

26
00:02:08.891 --> 00:02:13.810
Those who break rules must be punished, remember?"

27
00:02:13.811 --> 00:02:15.800
Bagheera shrugged.

28
00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:19.429
"Where can I find Hathi?" Mowgli asked.

29
00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.105
"Hathi?" Bagheera said.

30
00:02:22.106 --> 00:02:26.173
"I don't know. He feeds wherever he wants."

31
00:02:26.174 --> 00:02:28.846
"Can you find him and bring him to me?"

32
00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:31.919
Bagheera gave Mowgli a puzzled look.

33
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.483
"I can't give orders to the master of the jungle."

34
00:02:35.484 --> 00:02:40.760
"Please, Bagheera." Then Mowgli had an idea.

35
00:02:40.761 --> 00:02:47.179
"If Hathi won't come, say these words: the sacking of the fields.

36
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.586
Trust me, that will make him follow you."

37
00:02:51.587 --> 00:02:53.787
"'The sacking of the fields'?"

38
00:02:53.788 --> 00:02:57.659
Bagheera repeated the words until he remembered them.

39
00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:03.091
Then off he ran.

40
00:03:03.092 --> 00:03:06.799
It was dark when Bagheera finally returned.

41
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.264
To Mowgli's relief, Hathi was with him.

42
00:03:10.265 --> 00:03:15.286
The elephant's three sons trailed after them.

43
00:03:15.287 --> 00:03:19.619
"Hello, Mowgli!" Hathi called.

44
00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.730
Mowgli greeted the old elephant.

45
00:03:22.731 --> 00:03:25.231
Then he turned to Bagheera.

46
00:03:25.232 --> 00:03:31.465
"I'm going to tell you a story about a wise elephant," Mowgli said.

47
00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:36.303
Bagheera looked startled, but he gave Mowgli a nod.

48
00:03:36.304 --> 00:03:40.610
"This elephant once got caught in a hunter's trap."

49
00:03:40.611 --> 00:03:43.227
Mowgli glanced at Hathi.

50
00:03:43.228 --> 00:03:48.467
In the moonlight everyone could see a long white scar on his side.

51
00:03:48.468 --> 00:03:54.104
It looked as if someone had hit him with a red-hot whip.

52
00:03:54.105 --> 00:03:59.043
"Men came to take him from the trap," Mowgli continued.

53
00:03:59.044 --> 00:04:04.430
"But he was very strong and broke free of the ropes.

54
00:04:04.431 --> 00:04:09.139
He went away until his wound healed.

55
00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:15.618
Then one night he came back with some other elephants."

56
00:04:15.619 --> 00:04:19.736
He looked at Hathi. "What happened next?"

57
00:04:19.737 --> 00:04:21.743
Hathi finished the story.

58
00:04:21.744 --> 00:04:25.889
"We stomped on the men's fields.

59
00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.698
We ate their crops.

60
00:04:27.699 --> 00:04:31.547
We tore the roofs off their huts.

61
00:04:31.548 --> 00:04:34.656
And then . . ." He paused.

62
00:04:34.657 --> 00:04:38.737
"We let the wild jungle in.

63
00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:43.170
It grew back and swallowed up everything."

64
00:04:43.171 --> 00:04:46.286
Mowgli nodded, satisfied.

65
00:04:46.287 --> 00:04:49.680
The elephant swung his trunk to look at him.

66
00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:54.750
"How did you know about the sacking of the fields?"

67
00:04:54.751 --> 00:04:58.872
"Buldeo told that story one night," Mowgli said.

68
00:04:58.873 --> 00:05:02.580
"I guess he tells the truth once in a while."

69
00:05:02.581 --> 00:05:06.620
"What do you want from me?" Hathi asked.

70
00:05:06.621 --> 00:05:11.968
"The people living in this village are cruel," Mowgli explained.

71
00:05:11.969 --> 00:05:15.300
"They hurt Messua and her husband.

72
00:05:15.301 --> 00:05:17.483
They were planning to kill me.

73
00:05:17.484 --> 00:05:21.510
And then they were going to kill Messua with the red flower.

74
00:05:21.511 --> 00:05:25.287
It's only right to punish them."

75
00:05:25.288 --> 00:05:28.656
Bagheera shivered and dropped down low.

76
00:05:28.657 --> 00:05:35.270
Now he understood why Mowgli had sent for Hathi.
